3. Redistribution, source code and original-project credits

Every redistribution of the Software, whether modified or unmodified,
in source or executable form, must remain entirely Non-Commercial and
include this complete license and applicable copyright, attribution,
license, and third-party notices.

Every redistribution must credit the original MySearchWidget project
and include this repository URL in its credits:

https://github.com/alessio89g/MySearchWidget

The URL must be clickable when the medium supports links. Place this
credit in the existing credits or acknowledgments; if none exist, include
an accompanying CREDITS file. This obligation applies to both modified
and unmodified redistributions. A fork URL alone does not replace the
required reference to the original repository.

(a) Unmodified versions

If you redistribute a version without changes to its source code or
bundled application resources, including an unchanged official APK,
a link to the original repository in the credits is sufficient: you
are not required to deliver or separately host the Corresponding Source.
An otherwise unmodified build from the original source also qualifies;
changes solely to build-generated metadata or signing certificates do
not make it a modified version. Adding the license and credit notices
required by this section does not make a version modified.

(b) Modified versions and derivative works

If you redistribute a modified version or a derivative work, you must:

- include the complete Corresponding Source with the distributed copy,
  at no additional charge, either in the same archive or in an
  accompanying source archive delivered together with that copy;
- license your modifications and derivative works under this same
  license, without additional restrictions on its granted permissions;
- clearly identify the version as modified and describe the changes,
  including the date of modification; and
- retain the original-project credit and repository URL required above.

For modified versions, a link to the original repository or a fork,
a promise to provide source later, or an offer available only on request
does not replace the requirement to deliver the Corresponding Source.
For a source-only distribution, the distributed source itself satisfies
this requirement if it is complete as defined in section 1.

You may keep modifications private when you do not redistribute them.
This does not permit commercial use of private modifications. Independent
works merely distributed alongside the Software are not required to adopt
this license; their own licenses continue to apply.

